"""Bet Din cases 95-104: officers, oaths, jurisdiction, and displacement."""
from kehillah_docket_batch40_data import F

EXTRA_CASES_6 = [
 F(95,"BD-202","treasurer_trial","ally_on_bench","nezikin","The Communal Officer on Trial",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] accuses the communal treasurer of hiding a payment. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] offers to stand trial, but has named two close allies for the bench. The ledger is available; confidence in those who read it is not.",
   ["Accept the proposed bench and hear the account today.","Choose independent judges and audit the ledger.","Remove the treasurer before hearing the charge."],
   ["A friendly bench may clear its own patron.","New judges cost time, but their ruling can command trust.","An innocent officer could lose both office and reputation."],
   ["The treasurer's chosen bench hears the charge.","Independent judges take the ledger and hear both parties.","The treasurer is removed without a hearing."],
   "The proposed judges share a financial interest with the treasurer. Their acquittal could not settle the charge.","The ledger clears the treasurer. Removal punished an officer without cause.","Sanhedrin 3:4","the judges' interest in the account"),
 F(96,"BD-203","foreign_oath","words_misunderstood","nezikin","The Oath in an Unfamiliar Language",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] demands an oath over a disputed payment. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] will swear, but only in a language the clerk speaks poorly. The translator has not yet arrived. A solemn formula means little if its speaker and hearers understand different debts.",
   ["Take the oath as the clerk records it.","Wait for a trusted translator and restate the claim.","Reject the oath and award the claim."],
   ["The recorded words may say more than the speaker intended.","Translation delays collection but gives the oath a clear object.","A valid defense may be lost for a language barrier."],
   ["The clerk records the oath and the court closes the claim.","The court writes the exact claim in both languages before any oath.","The claimant wins without an oath."],
   "The clerk mistook a partial payment for a denial of all debt. The recorded oath answered the wrong claim.","The speaker understands the claim and can answer it. Refusal denied a meaningful defense.","Shevuot 7:1","what the oath's speaker understood"),
 F(97,"BD-204","one_sided_judge","private_advice_given","nezikin","The Judge Who Heard One Side",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] visited a judge before the hearing and described a disputed sale. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] now fears the judge has already advised the seller. The judge says the meeting was brief. The court must decide whether the coming hearing can still be trusted.",
   ["Keep the judge and proceed today.","Ask what was said and seat a replacement if needed.","Dismiss the sale claim as tainted."],
   ["A private consultation may already have shaped the bench.","Inquiry preserves a hearing while protecting its appearance of fairness.","The claimant may lose a valid claim for a judge's mistake."],
   ["The original judge hears the sale dispute.","The court records the meeting and appoints an uninvolved judge if advice was given.","The claim is dismissed before evidence is heard."],
   "The judge gave detailed advice about winning the case. Keeping that judge compromised the hearing.","The meeting concerned only scheduling. Dismissal punished the claimant without cause.","Pirkei Avot 1:8","the substance of the private meeting"),
 F(98,"BD-205","court_fee","fee_unapproved","nezikin","The Disputed Court Fee",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks the court to hear a small debt. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the clerk's newly demanded fee is larger than the debt itself. The clerk calls it a customary charge, but no schedule is posted.",
   ["Collect the fee before opening the case.","Hear the claim and inspect the fee account.","Abolish all hearing fees at once."],
   ["An unapproved charge can close the court to poorer neighbors.","Review costs time but keeps the claim accessible.","The court may lose a legitimate way to pay its clerk."],
   ["The clerk collects the demanded fee.","The claim is heard while the officers inspect fee approvals and costs.","All hearing fees are canceled."],
   "The clerk raised the fee without communal approval. Collection denied access on a private demand.","The posted schedule authorizes a modest fee. Blanket abolition leaves the clerk unpaid.","Sanhedrin 1:1","whether this fee was authorized"),
 F(99,"BD-206","border_captives","ransom_inflated","nashim","The Captives from a Border Raid",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] brings news of neighbors taken in a border raid. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] holds the relief purse and warns that the intermediary's price may rise if paid without question. Families want action before the captives are moved again.",
   ["Pay the full price immediately.","Fund contact and verify the captives and demand.","Refuse this demand and preserve the purse."],
   ["A hurried payment may reward an invented surcharge.","Verification costs precious time but gives families a credible path.","A real chance of release could vanish."],
   ["The court sends the full ransom through the intermediary.","The court funds contact, confirms names, and negotiates a documented price.","The court declines the demand."],
   "The intermediary added captives who were already free. Full payment wasted relief money.","The names and demand are genuine. Refusal leaves captives without a timely advocate.","Gittin 4:6","the captives' names and the demanded price","prosperity"),
 F(100,"BD-207","merchant_qadi","forum_promised","nezikin","The Merchant Before the Qadi",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] asks this court to settle a cargo debt. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] has already petitioned the qadi and says the contract named that forum. Parallel hearings could produce two answers to the same obligation.",
   ["Hear the case here and disregard the other petition.","Examine the contract and coordinate a single hearing.","Yield every claim to the qadi."],
   ["A promised forum may be ignored and rulings may conflict.","Review of the forum clause delays payment but protects both parties.","A communal claim may be abandoned without need."],
   ["The court issues its own cargo ruling.","The judges verify the forum clause and seek one recognized process.","The court declines every part of the claim."],
   "The parties expressly chose the qadi for this contract. A second ruling creates needless conflict.","No forum clause exists; both parties asked this court for relief. Automatic surrender abandoned them.","Sanhedrin 1:1","the contract's chosen forum"),
 F(101,"BD-208","lords_debt","receipt_valid","nezikin","The Christian Lord's Debt Claim",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] carries a lord's demand for repayment from [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName]. A seal is visible, but the borrower says a receipt was given to the lord's steward. The court's answer may travel beyond the community.",
   ["Pay the demand from communal funds.","Seek the steward's receipt and account for the seal.","Reject the lord's claim outright."],
   ["Payment may duplicate a settled debt.","A careful inquiry costs money but gives both sides a defensible record.","A valid debt could become a wider conflict."],
   ["The court pays the sealed demand.","The court requests the steward's account while preserving the claim.","The court refuses payment."],
   "The steward's receipt covers the debt. Immediate payment paid twice.","The receipt concerns another loan. Outright refusal leaves this debt unpaid.","Bava Metzia 1:6","whether the receipt covers this debt","prosperity"),
 F(102,"BD-209","converted_husband","property_reserved","nashim","The Converted Husband's Property",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] seeks household goods after a spouse's change of faith. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] holds the marriage agreement and says some goods were reserved separately. The neighbors' anger cannot tell the court who owns a chest.",
   ["Give the claimant all goods in the house.","Inventory the goods and read the marriage terms.","Leave every good with its current keeper."],
   ["A reserved dowry could be seized.","Inventory costs time and protects both property claims.","A clear claim could be lost through inaction."],
   ["All household goods pass to the claimant.","The court seals an inventory and compares each item with the marriage agreement.","Possession decides every item."],
   "The agreement reserves several goods to the other spouse. A blanket transfer takes their property.","The agreement assigns the disputed chest to the claimant. Leaving all goods in place ignores that term.","Kiddushin 4:1","the marriage agreement's property terms","prosperity"),
 F(103,"BD-210","refugee_loan","payment_record_found","nezikin","The Refugee's Unfinished Loan",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] lent money before both parties fled their town. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says part was repaid on the road; the old account book was scattered. The court must keep a debt from becoming either a windfall or an excuse.",
   ["Order the full balance paid now.","Reconstruct payments from witnesses and surviving notes.","Cancel the loan because the books are gone."],
   ["The borrower may pay a second time.","The inquiry costs a little while preserving a real claim.","Loss of records alone may erase an honest lender's due."],
   ["The borrower must pay the full claimed balance.","The court records a provisional balance and searches for payment evidence.","The loan is canceled."],
   "A travel note proves a substantial payment. The full award overcharges the borrower.","Witnesses confirm the principal remains due. Cancellation denies the lender's claim.","Bava Metzia 1:6","the payments made during flight","prosperity"),
 F(104,"BD-211","prisoner_release","release_promise_false","nashim","The Prisoner's Uncertain Release",
   "[kbd_litigant_a.GetFirstName] has collected money to release a detained neighbor. [kbd_litigant_b.GetFirstName] says the messenger's promise of release has no written guarantee. The prisoner may be moved tomorrow, but the communal purse cannot buy a rumor.",
   ["Send every coin with the messenger now.","Pay for a verified contact and stage the ransom.","Close the collection and return the gifts."],
   ["A false promise could consume the ransom fund.","Verification costs time and keeps the offer alive.","The prisoner may lose the only available route to release."],
   ["The full purse goes to the messenger.","The court confirms custody and releases funds against documented stages.","The collection is dissolved."],
   "The messenger has no authority to secure release. The full purse would be lost.","The custodian confirms a real release offer. Closing the collection abandons it.","Gittin 4:6","the messenger's authority and the prisoner's location","prosperity"),
]
